1
00:00:00,664 --> 00:00:04,018
In this tutorial,
I'll go over a few types of mounts.

2
00:00:04,504 --> 00:00:06,419
I'll cover the "basic free mount",

3
00:00:06,618 --> 00:00:09,852
the "kickup mount",

4
00:00:10,325 --> 00:00:13,737
the "side mount",

5
00:00:13,876 --> 00:00:17,290
and the "jump mount"
and "jump mount, seat out".

6
00:00:20,344 --> 00:00:23,218
How do you learn a basic mount?

7
00:00:23,670 --> 00:00:24,700
It's not that hard.

8
00:00:25,517 --> 00:00:28,347
To start, put the pedal at the bottom,

9
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:31,105
right or left, whichever you prefer.

10
00:00:31,290 --> 00:00:32,302
To get on,

11
00:00:32,668 --> 00:00:37,996
you press down on the bottom pedal
while pushing off with your back foot

12
00:00:38,295 --> 00:00:40,704
to get some momentum
and get on the unicycle.

13
00:00:40,770 --> 00:00:44,080
If you're not sure
which foot to start with,

14
00:00:44,424 --> 00:00:46,543
try it once on the right

15
00:00:46,614 --> 00:00:50,597
and once on the left, to see
which works best for you.

16
00:00:55,461 --> 00:00:59,548
For the "kickup mount", let's first see
how to place your feet.

17
00:01:00,001 --> 00:01:03,528
Position the unicycle
with the pedal at the bottom.

18
00:01:04,034 --> 00:01:06,309
Put your first foot
under the saddle

19
00:01:06,586 --> 00:01:09,161
and the other foot
on the sideways pedal

20
00:01:09,272 --> 00:01:12,555
so that foot's already in place
once you're on the unicycle.

21
00:01:13,227 --> 00:01:14,912
Now that your feet are in place,

22
00:01:14,998 --> 00:01:19,145
pull the saddle up
toward you as high as you can,

23
00:01:19,409 --> 00:01:21,941
so you can sit on it.

24
00:01:22,233 --> 00:01:25,940
Then put your other foot
on the other pedal.

25
00:01:30,301 --> 00:01:34,814
To start this "side mount",
stand the unicycle up next to you.

26
00:01:34,980 --> 00:01:37,794
Hold the middle of the saddle
for a better grip.

27
00:01:38,494 --> 00:01:41,841
Put the pedal closest to you
at the bottom.

28
00:01:42,047 --> 00:01:44,693
Next, cross your right leg

29
00:01:44,864 --> 00:01:49,714
in front of your left
and put your foot on the pedal.

30
00:01:50,214 --> 00:01:52,599
Tilt the unicycle slightly

31
00:01:52,665 --> 00:01:58,987
to leave room for your knee
when you lift it to get on.

32
00:01:59,413 --> 00:02:02,471
To get on, push down on the bottom pedal,

33
00:02:02,844 --> 00:02:08,634
then swing your other leg over the saddle
and onto the other pedal.

34
00:02:09,501 --> 00:02:11,842
Make sure you switch hands

35
00:02:11,940 --> 00:02:15,240
so you don't end up sitting
on the hand holding the saddle.

36
00:02:19,774 --> 00:02:23,470
For the "jump mount",
hold the front of the saddle

37
00:02:23,862 --> 00:02:26,640
to make room when you jump on.

38
00:02:27,307 --> 00:02:29,752
Put both pedals at the same height

39
00:02:30,357 --> 00:02:33,279
and jump high enough
to land on the saddle,

40
00:02:33,684 --> 00:02:37,080
making sure your feet
land on the pedals.

41
00:02:37,146 --> 00:02:43,721
[Music]

42
00:02:43,787 --> 00:02:45,355
For this "jump mount, seat out",

43
00:02:45,514 --> 00:02:51,249
it's just like the "jump mount"
you just saw, except this time

44
00:02:51,569 --> 00:02:56,440
you grab the back of the saddle
and jump straight onto the pedals.

45
00:02:59,414 --> 00:03:00,800
Your turn!

46
00:03:00,866 --> 00:03:07,199
[Music]
